1
00:00:05,068 --> 00:00:08,238
Hey, Konta, things are bad.
I might end up unemployed.

2
00:00:08,321 --> 00:00:09,447
<i>Then you can go.</i>

3
00:00:09,531 --> 00:00:11,199
To Grandma's villa!

4
00:00:11,282 --> 00:00:12,700
Shall we go then?

5
00:00:12,784 --> 00:00:14,035
On our…

6
00:00:14,119 --> 00:00:15,620
Vacation!

7
00:00:17,705 --> 00:00:19,249
Konta, look! The ocean!

8
00:00:19,332 --> 00:00:21,209
Wow, it's so close!

9
00:00:21,292 --> 00:00:23,753
<i>To think we would end up</i>
<i>spending a vacation together</i>

10
00:00:23,837 --> 00:00:26,381
<i>at such a wonderful seaside villa.</i>

11
00:00:26,464 --> 00:00:27,799
Konta, summer oranges!

12
00:00:27,882 --> 00:00:30,051
<i>I wonder if Grandma liked summer oranges.</i>

13
00:00:30,135 --> 00:00:30,927
Thank you, Grandma.

14
00:00:32,095 --> 00:00:36,141
<i>Nice to meet you.</i>
<i>I'm the caretaker, Nishigami.</i>

15
00:00:36,224 --> 00:00:37,851
S-So handsome.

16
00:00:37,934 --> 00:00:40,145
<i>Those villa grounds</i>
<i>are under your jurisdiction.</i>

17
00:00:40,228 --> 00:00:42,021
<i>You do know that in one month,</i>

18
00:00:42,105 --> 00:00:46,359
<i>a landslide caused by a massive typhoon</i>
<i>will kill all the residents, correct?</i>

19
00:00:50,238 --> 00:00:51,823
Wow!

20
00:00:51,906 --> 00:00:53,658
Hey, Konta!

21
00:00:53,741 --> 00:00:56,035
The ocean in the morning is so beautiful!

22
00:00:56,119 --> 00:00:57,871
-Morning.
-Morning.

23
00:00:58,997 --> 00:01:01,040
This is the best.

24
00:01:02,333 --> 00:01:04,836
I might just live here forever.

25
00:01:06,379 --> 00:01:08,631
I'll squeeze yesterday's summer oranges
and make you some juice!

26
00:01:08,715 --> 00:01:10,258
What? No way, those are sour!

27
00:01:10,341 --> 00:01:12,468
I'll make sure to put honey in it.

28
00:01:12,552 --> 00:01:14,512
You'll put honey in it?
You're so kind, Midori!

29
00:01:15,096 --> 00:01:16,472
You're so sweet.

30
00:01:23,855 --> 00:01:24,856
What?

31
00:01:26,107 --> 00:01:27,358
Who could that be?

32
00:01:28,818 --> 00:01:30,069
Yes?

33
00:01:31,571 --> 00:01:33,197
-We came.
-We came.

34
00:01:33,865 --> 00:01:34,949
What?!

35
00:01:36,701 --> 00:01:38,953
SIX MONTHS AGO

36
00:01:39,037 --> 00:01:42,916
Wow, a villa! That's amazing, you're rich!

37
00:01:42,999 --> 00:01:44,792
Is it near the ocean? Can you go by train?

38
00:01:44,876 --> 00:01:46,920
I want to go! When can I come?

39
00:01:47,003 --> 00:01:49,881
My dad gave me the key,
so we can use it anytime.

40
00:01:50,673 --> 00:01:53,760
But you two can't take
time off work, right?

41
00:01:53,843 --> 00:01:55,762
You don't have the same days off either.

42
00:01:55,845 --> 00:01:58,473
We've barely seen each other
since starting work.

43
00:01:58,556 --> 00:02:01,517
We used to be together
almost every day in college.

44
00:02:02,101 --> 00:02:05,605
But once you become an adult,
it's hard to make time for that.

45
00:02:05,688 --> 00:02:07,565
I'll just quit my part-time job.

46
00:02:07,649 --> 00:02:08,483
What?

47
00:02:08,566 --> 00:02:10,610
I was just thinking about quitting anyway.

48
00:02:10,693 --> 00:02:12,862
It just feels uncomfortable there somehow.

49
00:02:12,946 --> 00:02:14,447
No, Tsumugi.

50
00:02:14,530 --> 00:02:17,992
You really shouldn't choose jobs
based on comfort.

51
00:02:18,076 --> 00:02:20,286
We're 28, you know.

52
00:02:20,870 --> 00:02:24,332
My temp contract ends this month too,
so if I want to take a break, I can!

53
00:02:24,415 --> 00:02:27,293
Do you guys have any intention
of actually working?

54
00:02:27,377 --> 00:02:31,214
In this day and age,
isn't it foolish to work so hard?

55
00:02:31,297 --> 00:02:34,133
<i>The pay is low, prices are up…</i>

56
00:02:34,676 --> 00:02:37,095
It's fine for us
since we live with our parents,

57
00:02:37,178 --> 00:02:39,347
but it must be tough
for people living on their own.

58
00:02:39,430 --> 00:02:41,766
More and more people around me
are saying it's better

59
00:02:41,849 --> 00:02:43,851
to hunt for a husband
and just get married.

60
00:02:43,935 --> 00:02:48,856
Oh, I want to get married too.
I want to be a housewife!

61
00:02:49,524 --> 00:02:54,362
Apparently that's increasing in America,
and the "tradwife" phenomenon is popular.

62
00:02:54,445 --> 00:02:57,532
There could be hot guys
if it's a villa near the ocean.

63
00:02:57,615 --> 00:02:59,909
Oh, hot guys! I want to go so bad!

64
00:02:59,993 --> 00:03:01,536
Come on, now.

65
00:03:01,619 --> 00:03:03,621
Calm down, both of you.

66
00:03:07,458 --> 00:03:08,876
I quit my part-time job.

67
00:03:09,460 --> 00:03:10,920
My temp contract ended.

68
00:03:14,799 --> 00:03:18,886
So, all of us are unemployed,

69
00:03:19,554 --> 00:03:22,473
and on a vacation from life, right?

70
00:03:24,308 --> 00:03:25,351
Right?

71
00:03:26,269 --> 00:03:28,438
-Excuse us.
-Excuse us.

72
00:03:28,521 --> 00:03:31,190
Wow! What is this place?
It's absolutely amazing!

73
00:03:31,274 --> 00:03:32,275
Wait!

74
00:03:32,358 --> 00:03:35,069
-This is awesome!
-Don't drag your suitcase!

75
00:03:37,071 --> 00:03:38,197
Get us some alcohol.

76
00:03:38,281 --> 00:03:40,241
What? It's still morning!

77
00:03:40,783 --> 00:03:43,536
Huh? What? Are you Midori's friends?

78
00:03:43,619 --> 00:03:45,830
Oh, you haven't met them, right?

79
00:03:45,913 --> 00:03:48,750
They're my friends from college,
Tsumugi and Rinrin.

80
00:03:48,833 --> 00:03:50,209
Nice to meet you!

81
00:03:50,293 --> 00:03:53,296
You're an actor, aren't you?

82
00:03:53,379 --> 00:03:55,298
Midori's told us about you.

83
00:03:57,633 --> 00:03:59,093
Hello.

84
00:03:59,177 --> 00:04:01,554
I'm the actor and performer, Konta.

85
00:04:02,972 --> 00:04:05,516
Konta Hoshino.

86
00:04:08,144 --> 00:04:11,147
I heard from Midori
that you're mainly working as an extra.

87
00:04:11,230 --> 00:04:15,193
Well, extras live as the character too,
so they are actors. Just so you know.

88
00:04:15,276 --> 00:04:16,110
You're an extra.

89
00:04:16,194 --> 00:04:18,363
I'm an extra, but since I live
as the character, I'm an actor.

90
00:04:18,446 --> 00:04:20,615
-He's an extra!
-For me…

91
00:04:20,698 --> 00:04:22,200
-I'm more of a performer.
-Move.

92
00:04:22,283 --> 00:04:23,785
-Move!
-Hey!

93
00:04:23,868 --> 00:04:26,496
Here you go! Juice made
from the garden's summer oranges!

94
00:04:26,579 --> 00:04:28,122
-Wow!
-Yes!

95
00:04:28,206 --> 00:04:30,917
Thank you both for coming all this way!

96
00:04:32,251 --> 00:04:33,961
-Oh, it's good!
-Delicious!

97
00:04:34,045 --> 00:04:35,088
What is this?

98
00:04:35,171 --> 00:04:37,006
I'll add alcohol later
and make sours for you too.

99
00:04:37,090 --> 00:04:39,884
-Really?
-So! Let's have a barbecue tonight!

100
00:04:40,551 --> 00:04:42,678
-Yay!
-Vacations are the best!

101
00:04:42,762 --> 00:04:44,722
The best!

102
00:05:17,964 --> 00:05:19,090
Is it here? It's here.

103
00:05:19,882 --> 00:05:20,842
It's here.

104
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:23,970
It's here!

105
00:05:27,348 --> 00:05:29,851
Yes, this way, come along.

106
00:05:29,934 --> 00:05:31,060
This way.

107
00:05:31,144 --> 00:05:33,062
What? Someone else is here too?

108
00:05:33,146 --> 00:05:34,689
This is my friend, Tetsuro.

109
00:05:34,772 --> 00:05:37,984
He's the same age as me, 33. We met
way back when working part-time as movers.

110
00:05:38,067 --> 00:05:39,819
He's not an actor.

111
00:05:40,486 --> 00:05:41,904
Come on, Tetsuro. Help us out.

112
00:05:41,988 --> 00:05:43,698
A barbecue needs a man's strength!

113
00:05:43,781 --> 00:05:47,451
Wow, nice to meet you! I'm Rinrin.

114
00:05:47,535 --> 00:05:49,620
Stop flirting with everyone.

115
00:05:49,704 --> 00:05:52,790
Tetsuro, for now,
could you help over here?

116
00:05:52,874 --> 00:05:53,958
We need to start the fire--

117
00:05:54,041 --> 00:05:54,876
Oh, right!

118
00:05:54,959 --> 00:05:57,086
Could you pick up some branches
around here to burn?

119
00:05:57,170 --> 00:05:58,671
We have charcoal, but not firewood.

120
00:05:58,754 --> 00:06:00,548
All right, put your bag down.

121
00:06:00,631 --> 00:06:01,674
-Branches.
-Branches?

122
00:06:01,757 --> 00:06:03,092
-Yes, go on.
-Branches?

123
00:06:03,176 --> 00:06:04,427
Branches?

124
00:06:05,178 --> 00:06:06,095
Branches.

125
00:06:08,890 --> 00:06:10,016
He seems weird.

126
00:06:10,099 --> 00:06:11,058
He's an introvert.

127
00:06:11,142 --> 00:06:13,561
Is he staying here too?
He's kind of scary.

128
00:06:16,314 --> 00:06:17,273
Huh?

129
00:06:17,356 --> 00:06:18,191
What?

130
00:06:18,274 --> 00:06:20,443
Why won't it burn?

131
00:06:20,526 --> 00:06:22,570
It's impossible without something
like a fire starter.

132
00:06:22,653 --> 00:06:26,490
We bought charcoal at the store,
but you didn't buy a fire starter! Idiot!

133
00:06:27,283 --> 00:06:29,118
Don't call me an idiot!

134
00:06:29,202 --> 00:06:32,914
I haven't done many barbecues.
This is my first time starting a fire.

135
00:06:32,997 --> 00:06:35,166
Because for me, my acting work…

136
00:06:35,249 --> 00:06:36,667
I was busy with my acting

137
00:06:36,751 --> 00:06:39,253
so I didn't have time for this thing!
I was too busy acting.

138
00:06:39,337 --> 00:06:40,755
Liar!

139
00:06:40,838 --> 00:06:43,424
You were just lazing around
at our parents' house.

140
00:06:43,507 --> 00:06:46,761
Wait, you still live
with your parents at that age?

141
00:06:46,844 --> 00:06:48,638
What's wrong with that?
Their house is in Tokyo.

142
00:06:48,721 --> 00:06:49,931
It's convenient.

143
00:06:52,266 --> 00:06:53,976
I got the branches.

144
00:06:54,060 --> 00:06:56,687
Oh, nice. If we burn these
and get some momentum,

145
00:06:56,771 --> 00:06:57,605
it might work.

146
00:06:57,688 --> 00:06:58,564
These branches…

147
00:06:59,523 --> 00:07:01,901
He kind of seems like a good person.

148
00:07:01,984 --> 00:07:03,945
Maybe he's just shy.

149
00:07:04,028 --> 00:07:06,572
Let's make that guy
pick up branches forever from now on.

150
00:07:16,123 --> 00:07:17,416
Damn it!

151
00:07:18,501 --> 00:07:20,711
It won't catch fire!

152
00:07:20,795 --> 00:07:24,590
The meat and vegetables are all ready.
All we have to do is grill them!

153
00:07:24,674 --> 00:07:27,635
Konta, can't you even
get a fire going quickly?

154
00:07:27,718 --> 00:07:28,594
Midori, I'm sorry.

155
00:07:30,888 --> 00:07:31,722
Oh!

156
00:07:33,307 --> 00:07:34,308
Huh?

157
00:07:37,270 --> 00:07:40,481
More people are here.

158
00:07:40,565 --> 00:07:42,817
Oh, Mr. Nishigami! Perfect timing!

159
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:45,361
Help us start the fire!
We've been trying for a while,

160
00:07:45,444 --> 00:07:47,154
but it's impossible
without a fire starter.

161
00:07:47,238 --> 00:07:49,198
Midori, who is this handsome guy?

162
00:07:49,282 --> 00:07:51,325
Is he going to join our barbecue too?

163
00:07:51,409 --> 00:07:54,829
Oh, no, this is Mr. Nishigami,
who takes care of the villas around here.

164
00:07:54,912 --> 00:07:56,330
Mr. Nishigami!

165
00:07:58,666 --> 00:08:00,167
Nice to meet you, Mr. Nishigami.

166
00:08:00,251 --> 00:08:02,712
I'm Midori's best friend, Rinrin.

167
00:08:02,795 --> 00:08:04,589
I'm also her best friend, Tsumugi.

168
00:08:04,672 --> 00:08:06,924
Wait, you two are swooning too much!

169
00:08:07,008 --> 00:08:08,676
What will you have to drink?

170
00:08:08,759 --> 00:08:11,804
There's summer orange juice,
and we made a sour cocktail too.

171
00:08:11,887 --> 00:08:14,765
Wow, you're so tall. How tall are you?

172
00:08:14,849 --> 00:08:17,101
Come on, you two,
you're making him uncomfortable!

173
00:08:17,184 --> 00:08:19,061
-I'm going to go touch up my makeup.
-What?

174
00:08:19,145 --> 00:08:21,022
-Me too!
-Well, in that case…

175
00:08:21,105 --> 00:08:24,692
I'll get a summer orange sour for you.

176
00:08:24,775 --> 00:08:27,612
What the hell? In the end,
you're those types of women!

177
00:08:27,695 --> 00:08:30,197
Those types who judge a person
by their looks!

178
00:08:30,281 --> 00:08:32,283
Even though we're working so hard.

179
00:08:32,908 --> 00:08:36,329
Mr. Nishigami, do you have
a fire starter? I forgot to buy one!

180
00:08:36,412 --> 00:08:37,830
We must not have enough branches.

181
00:08:37,913 --> 00:08:39,540
Let's go pick some up! Let's go!

182
00:08:40,166 --> 00:08:43,294
Branches? More branches?

183
00:09:09,487 --> 00:09:10,488
Mr. Nishigami!

184
00:09:10,571 --> 00:09:13,115
Please have some summer orange sour.

185
00:09:13,199 --> 00:09:14,283
Here we go.

186
00:09:16,827 --> 00:09:19,288
Whoa! The fire is lit already.

187
00:09:19,372 --> 00:09:20,915
You're good.

188
00:09:20,998 --> 00:09:22,583
Thank you very much.

189
00:09:22,667 --> 00:09:23,584
Here.

190
00:09:25,002 --> 00:09:26,712
No thank you, I'm…

191
00:09:27,421 --> 00:09:31,759
It has a bit of alcohol in it,
but your work is done for today, right?

192
00:09:57,076 --> 00:09:58,536
Hey, no fair!

193
00:09:58,619 --> 00:10:02,206
I want to toast with him too.

194
00:10:02,289 --> 00:10:03,749
Let's drink!

195
00:10:03,833 --> 00:10:05,876
We're going to drink a ton tonight!

196
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:10,756
Wow, fire! Yes!

197
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:12,591
We don't need branches anymore.

198
00:10:12,675 --> 00:10:16,220
Mr. Nishigami! Thank you! Good job!

199
00:10:16,303 --> 00:10:18,097
Well then, everyone…

200
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:30,776
Cheers!

201
00:10:34,822 --> 00:10:36,407
-It's great!
-Let's eat.

202
00:10:36,490 --> 00:10:38,826
-Is the meat done?
-It's cooking.

203
00:10:38,909 --> 00:10:40,411
Here you go.

204
00:10:40,494 --> 00:10:41,996
Mr. Nishigami, have some.

205
00:10:42,079 --> 00:10:43,789
It's only cheap meat, though.

206
00:10:43,873 --> 00:10:46,041
-That's true.
-Wait a minute, everyone.

207
00:10:46,125 --> 00:10:47,543
Let's take a photo before we eat.

208
00:10:47,626 --> 00:10:50,254
-Yes, let's take a photo.
-Oh, nice!

209
00:10:50,337 --> 00:10:52,423
Mr. Nishigami, over here.

210
00:10:52,506 --> 00:10:56,093
-All right, let's go.
-Over here, like this.

211
00:10:56,177 --> 00:10:57,636
Everyone, line up.

212
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:59,305
-All right!
-Nice.

213
00:10:59,388 --> 00:11:01,724
-Wait, will we all fit?
-Is everyone in frame?

214
00:11:01,807 --> 00:11:03,684
-Front or back camera?
-Front.

215
00:11:03,768 --> 00:11:04,810
Front camera.

216
00:11:04,894 --> 00:11:05,895
Ten seconds.

217
00:11:05,978 --> 00:11:07,188
-Okay.
-Okay.

218
00:11:07,271 --> 00:11:09,565
-Ten seconds.
-Ten seconds, okay.

219
00:11:10,524 --> 00:11:13,736
Ten, nine, eight, seven,

220
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:17,490
six, five, four, three,

221
00:11:17,573 --> 00:11:19,283
two, one…

222
00:11:29,335 --> 00:11:31,795
Watch out!

223
00:11:32,379 --> 00:11:34,173
Villas are so fun.

224
00:11:36,383 --> 00:11:38,761
Tetsuro, what kind of work
are you doing now?

225
00:11:38,844 --> 00:11:42,306
When I have acting work,
I'm thinking of commuting from here,

226
00:11:42,389 --> 00:11:44,183
so you should come anytime too!

227
00:11:44,934 --> 00:11:47,561
You can't run a villa
without a man's strength.

228
00:11:47,645 --> 00:11:49,438
Pick up some firewood for me!

229
00:11:50,147 --> 00:11:53,484
I think I might stay
at this villa all summer too.

230
00:11:53,567 --> 00:11:56,362
A vacation from life, as they call it?

231
00:11:56,445 --> 00:11:59,031
Yes, we've been working hard
for a long time.

232
00:11:59,114 --> 00:12:00,407
We should rest once in a while.

233
00:12:00,491 --> 00:12:02,785
-Did you ever work hard?
-What?

234
00:12:02,868 --> 00:12:05,120
Maybe I should pick up firewood too.

235
00:12:05,871 --> 00:12:06,997
Exactly!

236
00:12:07,081 --> 00:12:09,500
Let's all spend this summer here together!

237
00:12:10,084 --> 00:12:13,295
It's fine to have that kind of summer
at least once in your life!

238
00:12:13,379 --> 00:12:17,299
I just happen to not have
any acting work right now.

239
00:12:17,383 --> 00:12:19,093
You're off all year round, more like it.

240
00:12:19,176 --> 00:12:21,220
I know you get an allowance from Dad.

241
00:12:21,303 --> 00:12:23,472
An actor has to keep their schedule open

242
00:12:23,556 --> 00:12:25,432
so they can take a big role
whenever it comes!

243
00:12:25,516 --> 00:12:27,268
Anyway! Here.

244
00:12:28,143 --> 00:12:31,522
To everyone's vacation from life,

245
00:12:32,231 --> 00:12:33,649
cheers!

246
00:12:33,732 --> 00:12:36,402
Cheers!

247
00:12:41,031 --> 00:12:42,324
Wait.

248
00:12:42,408 --> 00:12:43,867
Where's Mr. Nishigami?

249
00:13:03,679 --> 00:13:05,055
He's way too handsome.

250
00:13:10,686 --> 00:13:13,480
You know, Mr. Nishigami has a cool face,

251
00:13:13,564 --> 00:13:16,191
but the way he talks
is actually pretty cute.

252
00:13:16,692 --> 00:13:19,945
I wonder if he grew up
abroad or something?

253
00:13:20,029 --> 00:13:21,196
Maybe it's a dialect?

254
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:23,741
There are all kinds
of people in the world.

255
00:13:24,950 --> 00:13:29,955
Now then, with new members
turning up one after another,

256
00:13:30,039 --> 00:13:34,084
our fortune living in this villa is…

257
00:13:35,919 --> 00:13:37,421
The Grim Reaper.

258
00:13:47,097 --> 00:13:49,975
<i>Oh? There are more of them?</i>

259
00:13:52,436 --> 00:13:53,479
Yes.

260
00:13:54,021 --> 00:13:57,775
In addition to the two people I reported
last time, three more have come.

261
00:13:59,151 --> 00:14:01,737
And they will most likely…

262
00:14:04,615 --> 00:14:06,700
stay at the villa for the summer.

263
00:14:08,410 --> 00:14:09,787
<i>Grim Reaper.</i>

264
00:14:10,412 --> 00:14:14,750
<i>It's barely been a few decades</i>
<i>since you were assigned to Tatsumi Town,</i>

265
00:14:14,833 --> 00:14:18,003
<i>but before that, you spent</i>
<i>a lot of time in foreign countries.</i>

266
00:14:18,671 --> 00:14:21,382
Before Japan, I watched over the deceased

267
00:14:22,091 --> 00:14:25,177
for a long time in neighboring Korea.

268
00:14:26,303 --> 00:14:27,388
<i>How is it?</i>

269
00:14:27,471 --> 00:14:29,598
<i>Have you gotten used to the Japanese?</i>

270
00:14:30,766 --> 00:14:32,935
<i>Still, it is something to be envious of,</i>

271
00:14:33,018 --> 00:14:36,772
<i>considering we are handling</i>
<i>such heavy workloads every day like this.</i>

272
00:14:36,855 --> 00:14:39,441
<i>And this year will likely be even busier.</i>

273
00:14:41,026 --> 00:14:42,069
That is true.

274
00:14:43,112 --> 00:14:46,532
<i>At the end of summer,</i>
<i>this villa ground will be hit</i>

275
00:14:46,615 --> 00:14:49,535
<i>by a large-scale landslide</i>
<i>disaster due to a typhoon.</i>

276
00:14:49,618 --> 00:14:51,787
<i>Make sure to report the precise increase</i>

277
00:14:51,870 --> 00:14:54,623
<i>or decrease in the number</i>
<i>of casualties when that happens.</i>

278
00:14:54,707 --> 00:14:59,253
<i>Keep track of the people coming</i>
<i>and going from those villa grounds,</i>

279
00:14:59,837 --> 00:15:01,046
<i>Grim Reaper.</i>

280
00:15:03,799 --> 00:15:05,467
Yes, I understand.

281
00:15:06,176 --> 00:15:08,929
Until the moment
the flame of their lives goes out,

282
00:15:10,264 --> 00:15:12,391
I will watch over them closely.

283
00:15:19,398 --> 00:15:21,817
DOCTOR KENTARO SAWAMURA
EXTRAS WAITING AREA

284
00:15:23,277 --> 00:15:26,113
That's right. A villa in Tatsumi Town.

285
00:15:26,196 --> 00:15:28,073
Even when it comes to reading a script,

286
00:15:28,157 --> 00:15:30,242
just getting away
from the hustle and bustle of the city

287
00:15:30,325 --> 00:15:36,915
completely changes how you play the role,
or how you build the character, you know.

288
00:15:36,999 --> 00:15:38,500
Oh, really!

289
00:15:38,584 --> 00:15:39,752
The three of you are cute.

290
00:15:39,835 --> 00:15:41,295
I might fall in love today.

291
00:15:41,378 --> 00:15:43,213
Extras, it's almost time.

292
00:15:43,297 --> 00:15:44,465
-Okay!
-Thank you.

293
00:15:44,548 --> 00:15:45,382
Let's do this!

294
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:48,302
It looks like Mr. Jin can't come today.

295
00:15:48,385 --> 00:15:50,637
-What?
-What should we do?

296
00:15:50,721 --> 00:15:52,806
-What will we do?
-Why not?

297
00:15:56,852 --> 00:15:58,270
I'm sorry, everyone!

298
00:15:58,896 --> 00:16:04,276
Jin Ichijo suddenly can't come,
so today's shooting is canceled!

299
00:16:04,359 --> 00:16:06,236
What?

300
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:09,114
-I waited for five hours.
-I'm sorry.

301
00:16:09,198 --> 00:16:10,824
Seriously?

302
00:16:12,451 --> 00:16:16,663
Come on, it's not good to bail
when you're the main star.

303
00:16:17,456 --> 00:16:21,043
I wonder if Mr. Jin
caught a cold or something?

304
00:16:29,218 --> 00:16:32,221
Is it true that you have a villa
in Tatsumi Town?

305
00:16:34,807 --> 00:16:35,849
Mr. Jin?

306
00:16:36,391 --> 00:16:39,520
Can I go there too?

307
00:16:40,896 --> 00:16:42,147
You want to come?

308
00:16:42,898 --> 00:16:43,941
Yes.

309
00:17:05,337 --> 00:17:06,630
I'm the actor…

310
00:17:06,713 --> 00:17:07,965
I'm Jin Ichijo.

311
00:17:08,048 --> 00:17:09,883
Why is a celebrity
coming to a place like this?

312
00:17:09,967 --> 00:17:11,927
<i>A much longer break than you all.</i>

313
00:17:12,010 --> 00:17:14,888
Mr. Jin, don't say that, come on!
You're going to be fine!

314
00:17:14,972 --> 00:17:17,391
You're here on vacation, aren't you?

315
00:17:18,267 --> 00:17:19,560
Whoa!

316
00:17:20,269 --> 00:17:22,146
Are you going to eat those?

317
00:17:22,229 --> 00:17:24,606
<i>By the way, are you from overseas?</i>

318
00:17:24,690 --> 00:17:26,316
<i>The way you talk is just kind of…</i>

319
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:29,069
<i>I am with this publication.</i>

320
00:17:29,653 --> 00:17:30,779
What an absolute piece of garbage.

321
00:17:30,863 --> 00:17:32,656
<i>There's nowhere left</i>
<i>for him to go but hell.</i>

322
00:17:32,739 --> 00:17:34,533
Say it to my face!

323
00:17:34,616 --> 00:17:37,411
I'm just going to say it,
but you brought this entirely on yourself!

324
00:17:38,370 --> 00:17:39,621
No!

325
00:17:40,414 --> 00:17:41,373
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.

